  "worked_solution": "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overset{\u2015}{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma ,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\overset{\u2015}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma \n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=35.4,$ $z=-1.1,$ and $\\sigma =10.5$ into the formula and solving for $\\overset{\u2015}{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\overset{\u2015}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ 35.4 & =\\overset{\u2015}{x}+(-1.1)\\cdot 10.5 \\\\ 35.4 & =\\overset{\u2015}{x}-11.55 \\\\ \\overset{\u2015}{x} & =46.95.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
